.Dd May 28, 2026
.Dt XTC_TLS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_tls_ctx_create ,
.Nm xtc_tls_ctx_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_tls_create ,
.Nm xtc_tls_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_tls_handshake ,
.Nm xtc_tls_read ,
.Nm xtc_tls_write ,
.Nm xtc_tls_shutdown ,
.Nm xtc_tls_wants_read ,
.Nm xtc_tls_wants_write ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_version ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_cipher ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_cipher_bits ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_alpn_selected ,
.Nm xtc_tls_has_peer_cert ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_peer_subject_dn ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_peer_common_name ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_peer_issuer_dn ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_peer_serial ,
.Nm xtc_tls_get_server_cert_hash
.Nd TLS over async sockets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_tls.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_tls
provides TLS 1.2 / 1.3 over xtc_io sockets.  The implementation
selects a backend at configure time
.Pq Sq --with-tls=openssl|none|auto ;
in v0.x only OpenSSL is implemented.
.Pp
.Sy Per-connection state machine :
.Bl -tag -width "wants_write" -offset indent
.It Vt xtc_tls_ctx_t
Per-process state: cert, key, CA bundle, version range, ALPN
profile.  Created once via
.Fn xtc_tls_ctx_create
with role
.Pq Dv XTC_TLS_SERVER or Dv XTC_TLS_CLIENT
plus opts.
.It Vt xtc_tls_t
Per-connection state.  Wraps a single fd.  Created via
.Fn xtc_tls_create "ctx" "fd" "&out" .
.El
.Pp
.Sy Non-blocking handshake :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_tls_create(ctx, fd, &tls);
for (;;) {
    int rc = xtc_tls_handshake(tls);
    if (rc == XTC_OK) break;
    if (rc != XTC_E_AGAIN) abort();
    uint32_t want = xtc_tls_wants_read(tls)
                  ? XTC_IO_READABLE : XTC_IO_WRITABLE;
    xtc_proc_wait_fd(fd, want, -1, &revents);
}
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn xtc_tls_read
and
.Fn xtc_tls_write
follow the same pattern: return
.Dv XTC_OK
on progress,
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
when the fd needs more poll iterations.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_tls_shutdown
performs the bidirectional close-notify dance; same WANT_*
translation.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Vt xtc_tls_opts_t
fields:
.Bl -tag -width "verify_peer" -offset indent
.It Va cert_file , key_file
PEM paths for server-side certificate.
.It Va ca_file
PEM CA bundle for verifying the peer.
.It Va verify_peer
.Dv 1
to require + validate the peer's cert.
.It Va verify_peer_mode
Tri-state peer verification, taking precedence over
.Va verify_peer
when not
.Dv XTC_TLS_VERIFY_DEFAULT :
.Dv XTC_TLS_VERIFY_NONE ,
.Dv XTC_TLS_VERIFY_REQUEST
(request a client certificate but complete the handshake if none is
presented), or
.Dv XTC_TLS_VERIFY_REQUIRE .
.It Va alpn_protos
ALPN wire-form list.
.It Va min_version , max_version
.Dv XTC_TLS_VER_12
or
.Dv XTC_TLS_VER_13 .
.It Va cipher_list , ciphersuites_13 , groups
TLS 1.2 cipher list, TLS 1.3 ciphersuites, and key-exchange groups.
.It Va crl_file , crl_dir
CRL file / hashed directory; either enables full-chain revocation checking.
.It Va prefer_server_ciphers
Honor the server's cipher order over the client's.
.It Va passphrase_cb , passphrase_userdata
Supply the passphrase for an encrypted
.Va key_file
without an interactive prompt.
.El
.Pp
A server context is hardened by default (documented defaults, not knobs):
TLS renegotiation and compression are disabled, session tickets and the
session cache are off, and the moving-write-buffer mode required for
correct non-blocking sends is enabled.
.Sh INTROSPECTION
Valid only after
.Fn xtc_tls_handshake
returns
.Dv XTC_OK .
.Fn xtc_tls_get_version
and
.Fn xtc_tls_get_cipher
return the negotiated protocol version and cipher name (or
.Dv NULL ) ;
.Fn xtc_tls_get_cipher_bits
the symmetric key strength;
.Fn xtc_tls_get_alpn_selected
the negotiated ALPN protocol.
.Fn xtc_tls_has_peer_cert
reports whether the peer presented a certificate that passed
verification;
.Fn xtc_tls_get_peer_subject_dn ,
.Fn xtc_tls_get_peer_common_name ,
.Fn xtc_tls_get_peer_issuer_dn ,
and
.Fn xtc_tls_get_peer_serial
read the peer certificate (RFC 2253 DN, commonName, issuer DN, decimal
serial), rejecting an embedded NUL with
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL .
.Fn xtc_tls_get_server_cert_hash
returns the RFC 5929
.Sy tls-server-end-point
hash of the local certificate for SCRAM channel binding (MD5/SHA-1
signatures are hashed with SHA-256, otherwise the digest matching the
certificate's signature algorithm).
A backend that has not implemented these returns
.Dv NULL ,
.Dv 0 ,
or
.Dv XTC_E_NOSYS .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_io 3 ,
.Xr xtc_net 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 0.1.  See
.Pa docs/M_TLS.md
for backend pluggability planning.
